WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.366
Hi, I'm Anamika.

00:00:02.416 --> 00:00:06.347
This is Credora, my ExaThon India 2026 entry.

00:00:06.397 --> 00:00:12.983
Pre-approved loans for corporate customers, decided inside Exasol Personal.

00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:17.606
The bank has the data, in six systems, gathered by hand.

00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:27.504
One run, 1,000 companies, 530 approved, 1,168 crore rupees in offers, 17 seconds.

00:00:27.904 --> 00:00:34.635
Bank data read in place, 3rd party data via API, everyone reading as their own Exasol user.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:38.784
This is the live Exasol database in DbVisualizer.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.877
Every statement is audited.

00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:44.521
Each role, and the AI, has its own Exasol user.

00:00:44.571 --> 00:00:49.250
Oracle, MySQL and PostgreSQL come in through virtual schemas.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.826
One query joins Oracle, MySQL, PostgreSQL and the Exasol decision.

00:00:54.876 --> 00:00:59.578
Here is Ambika Technologies with its partners and its offer.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.638
Now the app, as the data scientist.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.276
Run analysis starts one Lua script in Exasol.

00:01:09.326 --> 00:01:18.071
It refreshes the virtual schemas, pulls CIBIL, GST and Account Aggregator data through UDFs, scores, decides and ranks.

00:01:18.121 --> 00:01:20.879
The console shows each statement live.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.364
Done.

00:01:23.414 --> 00:01:26.010
I publish it to loan operations.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.946
As loan operations, the Top 50 comes from a PREFERRING skyline in Exasol, with the SQL beside it.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.781
Each company goes to a relationship manager.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.502
As a relationship manager, I see only my 24 companies.

00:01:47.552 --> 00:01:49.694
Exasol filters by my user.

00:01:50.094 --> 00:01:52.620
Every offer has a negotiation limit.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.125
Vertex Specialty Chem took the loan, so I log it.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.453
Ask Credora is Claude, querying Exasol through the MCP server as my own AI user.

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:04.311
Off-topic gets turned down.

00:02:04.361 --> 00:02:07.406
Negotiation headroom comes back with the SQL.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.083
It reads the semantic view.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.217
Every answer shows its SQL.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.288
Last, the admin.

00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:17.882
The control room proves row-level security.

00:02:17.932 --> 00:02:26.075
The RM and its AI user get the same 120 rows, a second RM gets none, and a direct read is refused.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.103
Every statement lands in Exasol's audit log.

00:02:30.153 --> 00:02:32.755
Scheduled jobs run inside Exasol too.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.281
The code is public on GitHub, MIT licensed, with docs, diagrams and the changelog.

00:02:41.331 --> 00:02:42.979
The data is synthetic.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.295
One command deploys it to AWS.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.615
Credora is built on Exasol open source.

00:02:48.665 --> 00:02:54.422
Thanks to the Exasol team, the Exasol Personal Local Starter Kit and Exasol Personal.

00:02:54.472 --> 00:02:55.789
Thanks for watching.
